{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"0c0560b6b92ffdc4","name":"card_unit_beaufighter_tf_mk_x","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Legions/units/card_unit_beaufighter_tf_mk_x","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BEAUFIGHTER TF Mk X","text":"Any unit that attacks this unit takes 3 damage first.","flavorText":"The Bristol Beaufighter was a British heavy fighter aircraft that was introduced in 1940 and used by the RAF and the air forces of the British Commonwealth during WWII. The Beaufighter was slow and heavy, but rather maneuverable, and had space for radar which made it an excellent night fighter to counter German night time bombing raids. The aircraft would take on a variety of roles throughout the war and was used in anti-shipping, ground attack and long-range interdiction.  The Beaufighter TF Mk X variant was called “Torbeau”, and was a two seated torpedo fighter aircraft that had a Hercules XVII engine with cropped superchargers, which improved its low-altitude performance. A total of 5,928 Beaufighters were built, 2,231 of the TF Mk X variant.","faction":"Britain","type":"bomber","rarity":"Unique","cost":6,"operationCost":2,"attack":4,"defense":4},"defaults":{"Name":"card_unit_beaufighter_tf_mk_x","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_beaufighter_tf_mk_x_title","SourceString":"BEAUFIGHTER TF Mk X","LocalizedString":"BEAUFIGHTER TF Mk X"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":4,"defense":4,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_beaufighter_tf_mk_x_text","SourceString":"Any unit that attacks this unit takes 3 damage first.","LocalizedString":"Any unit that attacks this unit takes 3 damage first."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_beaufighter_tf_mk_x_history","SourceString":"The Bristol Beaufighter was a British heavy fighter aircraft that was introduced in 1940 and used by the RAF and the air forces of the British Commonwealth during WWII. The Beaufighter was slow and heavy, but rather maneuverable, and had space for radar which made it an excellent night fighter to counter German night time bombing raids. The aircraft would take on a variety of roles throughout the war and was used in anti-shipping, ground attack and long-range interdiction.  The Beaufighter TF Mk X variant was called “Torbeau”, and was a two seated torpedo fighter aircraft that had a Hercules XVII engine with cropped superchargers, which improved its low-altitude performance. A total of 5,928 Beaufighters were built, 2,231 of the TF Mk X variant.","LocalizedString":"The Bristol Beaufighter was a British heavy fighter aircraft that was introduced in 1940 and used by the RAF and the air forces of the British Commonwealth during WWII. The Beaufighter was slow and heavy, but rather maneuverable, and had space for radar which made it an excellent night fighter to counter German night time bombing raids. The aircraft would take on a variety of roles throughout the war and was used in anti-shipping, ground attack and long-range interdiction.  The Beaufighter TF Mk X variant was called “Torbeau”, and was a two seated torpedo fighter aircraft that had a Hercules XVII engine with cropped superchargers, which improved its low-altitude performance. A total of 5,928 Beaufighters were built, 2,231 of the TF Mk X variant."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardAttacks"],"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'au_aircraft_large'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Explosions_SFX/Cues/au_aircraft_large.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Invasion/t_beaufighter.t_beaufighter","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Doug Post","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/BEAUFIGHTER_TF_Mk_X.BEAUFIGHTER_TF_Mk_X","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto